From 619768ed268a529478e662e6c9240ae01b1b7e9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <winshyon@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:36:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] client: fail login if the config file cannot be saved

`celler login` saved the configuration when its ConfigWriteGuard was
dropped, which can only log errors. If the file could not be written
(or no config path could be determined), login still exited with
success and later commands failed with "No servers are available."

Add ConfigWriteGuard::save() to save explicitly and return errors,
make Config::save() fail when no config path is available, and use
it in `celler login`.

Fixes #75
